      "content": "Wait, what do you mean by \"goblin-friendly\" temperature? I just need the actual Celsius or Fahrenheit ranges that keep the lactobacillus and yeast in a stable ratio. Also, can you be a bit more specific about how the protein content in the flour affects the buffering capacity of the starter? I'm looking for the actual chemistry, not metaphors.",
